<title>AUSTRIA: IRAQ REPEATS EXPECTS OIL AID PLAN IN 7-10 DAYS.</title>
<headline>IRAQ REPEATS EXPECTS OIL AID PLAN IN 7-10 DAYS.</headline>
<text>
<p>VIENNA, June 26 (Reuter ) - Iraqi Oil Minister Amir Rasheed reiterated on Thursday that he expected an aid distribution plan that provides for renewed U.N.-supervised oil sales would be ready in about seven to 10 days.</p>
<p>He told a news briefing in Vienna that the plan would be finalised in &quot;a week or 10 days from now maximum..or possibly a couple of days more or less&quot;.  </p>
<p>New price formulas for the second phase of oil sales contracts would be available two to three days after the aid distribution plan was approved.</p>
<p>-- Vienna newsroom +431 713 2002</p>
</text>
